<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The X3 speaks PLAIN HTTP, and since targetSdk 28 Android refuses that by
  default. targetSdk is 35 here, so every request the Insta360 SDK makes to
  http://192.168.42.1 was being blocked by the platform before it reached the
  Wi-Fi — no packet, no timeout, just a refusal that surfaces as a connect
  error with no hint of its cause.

  This is a SECOND, INDEPENDENT cause of the same failure as the Wi-Fi bind in
  X3Bridge.kt, and fixing either alone leaves the other in place: bind the
  process to the camera's network and cleartext is still blocked; permit
  cleartext and the sockets still leave over mobile data.

  Scoped to the camera's address ON PURPOSE rather than a blanket
  usesCleartextTraffic="true". Everything else this app talks to is our own
  bench over HTTPS, and a global opt-out would quietly permit an unencrypted
  fallback for all of it. One host is the whole exposure.

  192.168.42.1 is the X3's own gateway when the phone joins its access point.
  It is fixed by the camera, not configurable, which is why it can be written
  here as a literal.

  This file ships ONLY with the camera build — the public SDK-free APK keeps
  Android's strict default, correctly, since it never talks to a camera.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">192.168.42.1</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
